Usage of Eire as the name for the State is obsolete, since The Republic of
Ireland Act, 1948.  So as of now, it is technically incorrect (although
not uncommon) for the State to be referred to as Eire.  And even prior to
1948, when Eire was an official name for the State, and in current
common usage, it was and is also a name for the island as a whole, which is
what I meant when I originally said "not just the Republic of Ireland".

Reference: <http://www.irishstatutebook.ie/ZZA22Y1948S2.html>.


